{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782045196626,"sessionID":"ses_115d49226ffePMDD7oOsMwXDCx","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-8f253c352aa13017","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"[package]\nname = \"book-api\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\n\n[dependencies]\naxum = \"0.7\"\ntokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"full\"] }\nserde = { version = \"1\", features = [\"derive\"] }\nserde_json = \"1\"\nrusqlite = { version = \"0.31\", features = [\"bundled\"] }\nr2d2 = \"0.8\"\nr2d2_sqlite = \"0.24\"\ntower = { version = \"0.5\", features = [\"util\"] }\nhttp-body-util = \"0.1\"\nmime = \"0.3\"\n\n[dev-dependencies]\ntower = { version = \"0.5\", features = [\"util\"] }\ntokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"full\", \"test-util\"] }\n","filePath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-wicr10cv/retort-30c843755bb3/Cargo.toml"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-wicr10cv/retort-30c843755bb3/Cargo.toml","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"Cargo.toml","time":{"start":1782045196617,"end":1782045196624}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me set up an axum-based REST API with SQLite. I'll use rusqlite (synchronous, simpler) or sqlx. Let me use rusqlite with a mutex for simplicity since we don't have network dependencies issue. Actually, axum is async — better to use sqlx with async sqlite, but rusqlite with tokio task blocking works fine too. Let me use rusqlite + tokio with spawn_blocking wrapped in a Mutex, or simpler: use `r2d2_sqlite` connection pool.\n\nActually let me use axum + sqlx with sqlite. sqlx requires offline mode or a database URL. Using `sqlx::sqlite::SqlitePool` with in-memory or file. For tests, in-memory is tricky. Let me use rusqlite with a Mutex, simpler.\n\nPlan:\n- Cargo.toml with axum, tokio, serde, serde_json, rusqlite, r2d2, r2d2_sqlite, tower (for tests), hyper.\n- main.rs: setup router, pool, state\n- handlers in separate modules\n- tests in tests/\n\nLet me write it.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eea2bb8f4001W2qxCAqQcGkFo7","sessionID":"ses_115d49226ffePMDD7oOsMwXDCx","messageID":"msg_eea2b9345001Q35zqSAcPGBDCp"}}
